      "rationale": "Density of medical terminology is a plausible proxy for clinical complexity relevant to visit length. However the counts are suspiciously high (20-28 per short note) and near-constant across rows, suggesting an opaque/over-broad term definition that weakens both leverage and clear groundedness, though values are broadly defensible."
    },
    {
      "name": "comorbidity_count",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Comorbidity burden is a genuinely useful clinical axis for predicting visit duration. But groundedness is shaky: the annual-physical row (no stated comorbidity, just mild fatigue) and the pediatric viral URI row are both marked comorbidity_count=1, which the text does not clearly support, indicating over-attribution."
    },
    {
      "name": "action_count",
